Sval: about:logging and about:memory write no file while a private window is open

Gecko's logging names the addresses it works on, and about:memory's saved
reports and its GC and CC logs name each document by its address. A private
window leaves nothing on disk, so about:logging cannot start logging or set
a log file or modules while one is open, and about:memory's Measure and
save and both Save GC & CC logs buttons are disabled. SvalProfiler holds the
buttons and stops logging that runs when a private window opens;
about:logging follows that stop.

